  "capacityNotes": [
    "Database: 16 GiB preserves the current 5.7 GiB shared_buffers setting. Four vCPUs cap bursts below the observed 6.39-vCPU hourly maximum. Credit, replay and load checks are required before launch.",
    "Application services remain separate with individual task roles on a shared ECS EC2 host. The sum of independent hourly memory maxima was 2.12 GB; mean CPU was 0.157 vCPU. These are devnet shadow sizing observations, not a mainnet load test.",
    "Separate KMS keys and task roles are preserved, but co-located containers do not provide Fargate VM isolation. Host IMDS blocking, unprivileged tasks, distinct execution roles, resource controls and image validation are required.",
    "One database and one application node: replacement/restart does not provide an automatic database standby or guarantee zero downtime.",
    "Daily regional snapshots and logical dumps: 35-day current-backup retention, plus versioned-object lifecycle. Cross-region backup replication is not included. An S3 gateway endpoint keeps backup uploads off the NAT path."
  ],
  "excluded": [
    "Tax",
    "Vercel",
    "Existing Helius and Cloudflare subscriptions",
    "Solana worker funding/transaction fees",
    "Paid AWS Support",
    "New subscriptions or protocol deployment"
  ],
  "pricingCaveats": [
    "On-demand Linux x86 rates; no commitments, Spot, startup credits or discounts assumed.",
    "Variable usage quantities are explicit launch assumptions. Mainnet activity can exceed them. USD 400 is a planning amount, not a hard spending cap.",
    "The estimate includes the five existing KMS keys; their storage is already chargeable independently of this migration.",
    "An exportable database certificate costs USD 7 upon issuance and renewal. The monthly model carries a USD 2 reserve; the first month replaces that reserve with the USD 7 issuance fee."
  ]
